        <paragraph>The meaning of the decimal representation of a number $$0.d_{1}d_{2}d_{3}\ldots$$ (where the digit $$d_{i}$$ is one of the numbers $$0,1,2,\ldots,9$$ ) is that</paragraph>
        <paragraph math="block">$$0.d_{1}d_{2}d_{3}d_{4}\ldots = \frac{d_{1}}{10} + \frac{d_{2}}{10^{2}} + \frac{d_{3}}{10^{3}} + \frac{d_{4}}{10^{4}} + \cdots$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>Show that this series converges for all choices of $$d_{1},d_{2},\ldots$$ .</paragraph>
