      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="55" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Let $$\sum a_{n}$$ and $$\sum b_{n}$$ be series with positive terms. Is each of the following statements true or false? If the statement is false, give an example that disproves the statement.</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>If $$\sum a_{n}$$ and $$\sum b_{n}$$ are divergent, then $$\sum a_{n}b_{n}$$ is divergent.</item>
          <item>If $$\sum a_{n}$$ converges and $$\sum b_{n}$$ diverges, then $$\sum a_{n}b_{n}$$ diverges.</item>
          <item>If $$\sum a_{n}$$ and $$\sum b_{n}$$ are convergent, then $$\sum a_{n}b_{n}$$ is convergent.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>False</paragraph>
        <paragraph>False</paragraph>
        <paragraph>True</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
